<p>A two-week ceasefire between the United States and Iran remained formally in place on April 9, but it came under immediate strain after Israel intensified strikes on Lebanon and Iran again restricted tanker traffic through the Strait of Hormuz. U.S. officials, including President Trump and Vice President JD Vance, said the truce does not cover Lebanon. Iranian officials argued that Lebanon was part of the understanding, or that the Israeli attacks violated the deal. That gap over Lebanon has become the central test of whether the pause can lead to broader negotiations. Several reports say Pakistan helped broker the ceasefire and is expected to host further talks, while Washington has warned it will keep military forces in and around Iran until a &quot;real agreement&quot; is reached. Even with the tension, the ceasefire has so far halted broad direct U.S.-Iran attacks, leaving at least a narrow opening for diplomacy if the dispute over Lebanon and shipping can be contained. The human cost in Lebanon has been severe. Multiple outlets reported that Israeli strikes killed at least 182 people nationwide, while other reports put the toll at 254, with hundreds more wounded. The attacks drew condemnation from the United Nations and calls from European leaders to extend the ceasefire to Lebanon.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/DxTjxTlAR3tFu_HCWa98YmO7K4x2qp3L2tETwC4V_n8qavdPKoLtFEURNKrr_O4dN6zRVojxXhJFCWQSlLhLLUvi30OKoaz1qxR3n9Gbu31rfKTfDxtCF0DmmuSNFliaBXHwQS4fyg-Ekpc4p2AznR1V9hEo1YDCnnvSGt93W8i5r0v2wvwLzxX5okYSpgMbYcuSMs3gt3xtikcA_qthN0Fp-O1-VqC04rKRjVw' alt='Emergency crews attempt to rescue a man trapped in a car after an Israeli strike in Beirut.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>April 11 test: Reports say Washington and Tehran are heading into follow-up talks with sharply different agendas, underlining that the ceasefire paused fighting without settling the main terms of a longer deal.</li><li>Israeli strategy: Reuters-based reporting says Israel is carving out buffer zones in Gaza, Syria, and now Lebanon, suggesting it is preparing for a longer regional conflict even as Washington pushes diplomacy.</li><li>Shipping dispute: Britain is pushing for toll-free passage through the Strait of Hormuz as Tehran seeks tighter control over access, turning commercial transit into a parallel diplomatic fight.</li><li>Victory narratives: Both Washington and Tehran have claimed victory from the same ceasefire, a political dynamic that can make compromise harder in the next round of negotiations.</li><li>Urban exposure: Reports said strikes hit busy commercial and residential areas in central Beirut without warning, showing how quickly the Lebanon front spilled back into dense civilian spaces.</li></ul><blockquote>I think the Iranians thought that the ceasefire included Lebanon, and it just didn&#x27;t. - JD Vance</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Trump administration: President Trump called Israeli strikes on Lebanon a &quot;separate skirmish&quot; and said U.S. forces would remain deployed near Iran until a fuller agreement is honored. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/trump-says-israeli-strikes-on-lebanon-a-separate-skirmish-not-part-of-iran-ceasefire'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Iranian leadership: Iranian officials said Lebanon was part of the ceasefire understanding, or that attacks there amounted to violations, and Tehran signaled it would be unreasonable to continue talks under those conditions. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/08/world/middleeast/us-iran-israel-lebanon-cease-fire.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Israeli government: Israeli leaders said their campaign against Hezbollah in Lebanon continues independently of the Iran truce, arguing that their war aims are not complete. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/08/2026/israels-netanyahu-says-iran-ceasefire-is-not-end-of-the-war'>Semafor</a>)</li><li>Pakistan: Multiple outlets described Islamabad as the main intermediary in the last-minute diplomacy and the expected venue for the next round of U.S.-Iran talks. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/how-trump-went-from-threatening-irans-annihilation-to-agreeing-to-a-two-week-ceasefire-in-a-day'>PBS NewsHour</a>, <a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/ceasefire-iran-war-pakistan-negotiations-trump-lebanon/33727932.html'>Radio Free Europe/Radio Liberty</a>)</li><li>Israeli opposition: Opposition leader Yair Lapid called the ceasefire a &quot;political disaster,&quot; saying Israel was not even close to the table when decisions about its core national security were made. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/israel-opposition-leaders-slam-netanyahu-over-ceasefire-with-iran/article70839244.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>White House: Press secretary Karoline Leavitt said Trump and Netanyahu would keep discussing whether Lebanon might eventually be folded into a ceasefire arrangement. (<a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330456642/trump-will-continue-to-discuss-lebanon-with-israeli-pm-white-house'>Aaj TV</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/u-s-iran-ceasefire-tested-by-strait-of-hormuz-tension-and-israels-war-in-lebanon'>U.S.-Iran ceasefire tested by Strait of Hormuz tension and Israel&#x27;s war in Lebanon</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/ceasefire-iran-war-pakistan-negotiations-trump-lebanon/33727932.html'>Trump Says US Military To Remain Near Iran Until &#x27;Real Agreement&#x27; Reached</a> - rferl.org</li><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/04/08/iran-re-closes-strait-of-hormuz-after-israeli-strikes-in-lebanon-putting-ceasefire-at-risk'>Iran re-closes Strait of Hormuz after Israeli strikes in Lebanon, putting ceasefire at risk</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/4/9/us-vp-jd-vance-says-lebanon-is-not-part-of-the-us-iran-ceasefire'>US VP JD Vance says Lebanon is not part of the US-Iran ceasefire</a> - aljaze